    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] The 7th Asian Games (Persian: بازی‌های آسیایی ۱۹۷۴‎ ‎ ) were held from September 1, 1974, to September 16, 1974, in Tehran, Iran.\n[2] The Asian Games were hosted in the Middle East for the first time.\n[3] Apart from his World championship title, Al-Mudhaf also collected fourteen more medals to his career record, including two from the Asian Games (a silver in Guangzhou 2010 and a bronze in Doha 2006).\n[4] He was one of the athletes to win medals in two events in successive Asian Games, the bronze in the decathlon in the Tehran Asian Games in 1974 and a gold in the long jump in the Bangkok Asian Games, 1978."
